    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d383">

                <pb facs="0498" n="418" xml:id="pg418"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Adee to Mr.
                            de Margerie</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-08-11"><hi rendition="#italic">August 11,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 496.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inform you that your
                    telegram of the 7th instant was at once sent to the Navy Department, and that
                    that Department has instructed the commanding’ officer of the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Machias</hi> to act in his discretion to prevent any
                    destructive or injurious act against foreign interests or property in Haiti not
                    in the line of hostilities.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvey A. Adee</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
